---
import Docs from '../../layouts/Docs.astro';
import StatusDemo from '../../components/StatusDemo';
import CodeBlock from '../../components/CodeBlock.astro';
---

<Docs title="Status" description="A small round mark for the state of a task, run, or step.">
  <h1 class="docs-title">Status</h1>
  <p class="docs-lead">
    Shows where a task, run, or step stands: pending, running, paused, succeeded, warning, failed, stopped, or skipped.
    Running fills eight segments as a known amount grows, or spins like Spinner when the amount is unknown. For a
    page-level wait, use Progress or Spinner.
  </p>
  <div class="mt-8">
    <StatusDemo client:load />
  </div>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Usage</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="Status usage"
      code={`import { Status } from "@tulipfarm/sprout/status";

<Status state="pending" />
<Status state="running" />
<Status state="running" value={40} />
<Status state="success" />
<Status state="error" size="lg" />`}
    />
    <ul>
      <li>
        <code>state</code>: <code>pending</code> (default), <code>running</code>, <code>paused</code>,
        <code>success</code>, <code>warning</code>, <code>error</code>, <code>stopped</code>, or <code>skipped</code>.
      </li>
      <li>
        <code>value</code>: for <code>running</code>, a number from 0 to 100 fills a ring of eight green segments, one
        per 12.5%, and the segment being worked on fades in and out. Leave it out (or pass <code>null</code>) while the
        amount is unknown, and a blue line runs around the ring at the same speed as Spinner.
      </li>
      <li>
        <code>size</code>: <code>sm</code> (12px), <code>md</code> (16px, default), or <code>lg</code> (20px).
      </li>
      <li>
        <code>tooltip</code>: shown on hover. Defaults to the state’s name, such as “Succeeded” or “Running, 40%”. Pass
        your own words, such as <code>tooltip="Access denied"</code>, or <code>false</code> for none.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      The root gets <code>data-state</code>, <code>data-size</code>, and <code>data-determinate</code> while a running
      amount is known.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Motion</h2>
    <p>
      The mark scales in over 280ms when it mounts, and again whenever its state changes; the check, cross, or bar then
      draws in. A changing amount only fills the next segment, over 180ms. On hover with a mouse, the mark grows a
      little and its glyph draws again. With reduced motion, the mark only fades in, the line rests at the top, and the
      active segment stays half lit instead of fading.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Accessibility</h2>
    <p>
      Status is an <code>img</code> named after its state, such as “Succeeded” or “Running, 40%”. Pass{' '}
      <code>aria-label</code> to name it yourself, or <code>aria-hidden="true"</code> when text beside it already says
      the state. It is not a live region; put a <code>role="status"</code> summary nearby when a change should be
      announced. Color is never the only signal: each state has its own shape.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Theme tokens</h2>
    <p>
      Running uses <code>--sprout-info</code>, a known amount and success <code>--sprout-success</code>, warning{' '}
      <code>--sprout-warning</code>, and error <code>--sprout-danger</code>. Pending, paused, stopped, and skipped use{' '}
      <code>--sprout-muted</code>. Glyphs on a filled circle use <code>--sprout-surface</code>. In forced colors, the
      mark uses <code>CanvasText</code>, and running uses <code>Highlight</code>.
    </p>
  </section>
</Docs>
